{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CdSrjegYx4JyVo1bu6bm7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EUbJGU7aQBzRUx75cwM8d7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nAdd live SMA trend filter, fix sweep baseline bug, tune take-profit for real profitability\n\ncandidate_from_base() hardcoded min_entry_price=0 for the sweep's \"current config\"\nbaseline even though min_entry_price=50 has been a live filter in\nanalyze_and_trade.py since the WHEEL fix commit — every prior leaderboard was\ncomparing candidates against a baseline that didn't match production. With the\nbaseline corrected, a full 300-iteration sweep plus an exhaustive local grid\nsearch around it both converge on the same single change: raising\ntrailing_stop.take_profit_pct from 0.06 to 0.12 lets winners run instead of\ncapping them early, flipping the real 25-trade historical replay from -$178 to\n+$550 net P&L with no reduction in sample size.\n\nAlso wires up the SMA trend filter (get_sma in core/alpaca.py, sma_as_of/\nprefetch_sma_bars in backtest/trend.py) as a sweepable/live lever, disabled by\ndefault (trend_filter_sma_days=0) — enabling it in this backtest period cuts\nthe real-trade sample from 34 to 13, too small to trust yet.\n\nNo parameter combination found in the sweep passes the strict\n\"positive-every-month\" bar — a single April gap-down (GLW, -14% in 3 days)\nproduces an unavoidable stop-loss under every trailing-stop configuration\ntested. Profitability improved; a literal guarantee that every buy profits on\nsell is not achievable via trailing-stop tuning alone.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\ngit log --oneline -3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":113806,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemera